<title>EGYPT: National Cement profits sharply down.</title>
<headline>National Cement profits sharply down.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Majority state owned National Cement said on Sunday it made a net profit of 20.334 million pounds ($5.98 million) in the financial year 1995/6, over 60 percent down on 52.064 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>The financial year starts on July 1.</p>
<p>An official source earlier this month said the firm made an attributed profit of 3.9 million pounds ($1.1 million) in the financial year 1995/6.</p>
<p>The audited profit is equivalent to 0.296 pounds for each of the 68.8 million National Cement shares, which last traded on the Egyptian stock exchange at 17.00 pounds a share.</p>
<p>The company is one of the few cement firms which has not undergone large-scale privatisation. The state continues to hold an overwhelming stake but a few shares are in private hands.</p>
<p>The company's production of cement fell slightly to 1.901 million tonnes in 95/96 from 2.106 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>Here are details of the company's audited financial statements for the years 94/95 and 95/96 and its balance sheets at the end of the two years (all figures in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>				   94/95	    95/96</p>
<p>Sales			    352.662	  337.562</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>    Costs			270.234	  274.692</p>
<p>Net after-tax profits	 52.064	   20.334</p>
<p>				   30JUNE95		   30JUNE96</p>
<p>TOTAL LONG-TERM ASSETS     1,038.581		  1,039.977</p>
<p>including:</p>
<p>    Fixed assets		    610.863		 562.654</p>
<p>    Unfinished Projects	   406.536		 455.759</p>
<p>TOTAL CURRENT ASSETS		491.251		 514.233</p>
<p>including:</p>
<p>    Stock			     205.321		 273.719</p>
<p>    Debtors			   220.829		 166.035</p>
<p>TOTAL CURRENT LIABILITIES	 343.159		 345.215</p>
<p>including:</p>
<p>    Creditors			 286.181		 319.008</p>
<p>WORKING CAPITAL		     148.092		 169.018</p>
<p>TOTAL INVESTMENTS		 1,186.673	     1,208.995</p>
<p>SHAREHOLDERS' RIGHTS		 78.137		 101.615</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>    Paid-in capital		 137.600		 137.600</p>
<p>    Reserves			   44.681		  47.825</p>
<p>    (less deferred deficit     -104.144		 -83.810)</p>
<p>TOTAL LONG-TERM LIABILITIES   1,108.537	     1,107.380</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>    Loans			     443.724		 418.143</p>
<p>    Creditor banks		  664.813		 689.237</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
